# nest-scaffold command reference

This project already exists — you will only ever run `generate` subcommands
here, never `create`. All commands run from the project root via the local
devDependency:

```bash
npx nest-scaffold generate module <name> --full
npx nest-scaffold g m <name> --full          # alias
```

## generate module (alias m)

```bash
npx nest-scaffold generate module orders --full
{{#if moduleVersioning}}npx nest-scaffold g m orders --full --module-version v2
{{/if}}```

| Option | Effect |
|---|---|
| `--full` | Full CRUD: controller + service + DTOs + entity |
{{#if moduleVersioning}}| `--module-version <v>` | Target a specific version folder (this project has versioning enabled: {{moduleVersions}}) |
{{/if}}

Without `--full`, only a minimal module class is created.{{#if isMicroservice}} A
`--full` module on this microservice project also creates and registers a
`.proto` file automatically.{{/if}}

## generate service / generate controller (aliases s / c)

```bash
npx nest-scaffold g s orders
npx nest-scaffold g c orders
```

Adds a standalone service or controller to a module missing one.{{#if isMicroservice}}
On this microservice project, `generate controller` also creates the
module's `.proto` file and registers its gRPC package.{{/if}}

## generate method (alias me) — the command you'll use most

```bash
{{#if isMicroservice}}npx nest-scaffold g me orders approve --type patch
npx nest-scaffold g me orders findByStatus --type get --get-mode all
{{else}}npx nest-scaffold g me users findByEmail --type get --get-mode one --field email
npx nest-scaffold g me users findAllActive --type get --get-mode all
npx nest-scaffold g me orders approve --type patch
{{/if}}```

| Option | Effect |
|---|---|
| `--type <get\|post\|put\|patch\|delete>` | {{#if isMicroservice}}RPC shape{{else}}HTTP verb{{/if}} |
| `--get-mode <all\|one>` | For `get` only — list vs. single-record lookup |
| `--field <name>` | For `get --get-mode one` — lookup field (e.g. `email`, `slug`) |
{{#if moduleVersioning}}| `--module-version <v>` | Target a specific version folder |
{{/if}}

Patches the existing controller + service{{#if isMicroservice}} + `.proto`{{/if}}
in place. Leaves the method body as a TODO-style stub — it scaffolds shape,
not your domain logic. Never overwrites a method with the same name in
place; if the name collides it asks for a different one instead.

## Config

This project's `nest-scaffold.config.json` records architecture
(`{{architecture}}`){{#if moduleVersioning}}, module versioning (enabled,
default `{{defaultModuleVersion}}`){{else}}, module versioning
(disabled){{/if}}, and enabled features. `generate` reads it automatically —
you never need to repeat flags it can infer.
